<div class="wrap"><div class="known-gap-note"><strong data-i18n="missingTitle">Known ballots with unavailable timing.</strong> <span data-i18n="missingCopy">Official bulletins account for 454 ballots in two domestic sections and 831 ballots in 29 overseas tabulation sections without individual cast times. Another 41 overseas sections were not installed and contributed no ballots.</span> <a href="/data/missing-logs.json" target="_blank" data-i18n="missingSource">See the complete 72-section inventory ↗</a></div></div>
  <section id="coverage" class="wrap coverage-section"><div class="coverage-title"><div class="panel-kicker" data-i18n="coverageKicker">DATA COVERAGE</div><h2 data-i18n="coverageTitle">Data coverage and reconciliation</h2><p data-i18n="coverageCopy">These figures describe the logs analysed in this snapshot. Unavailable or unreconciled sections are visible in the coverage, not silently treated as zero.</p><div class="snapshot-date" id="snapshot-date"></div></div><div class="coverage-card"><div class="coverage-main"><span data-i18n="analysedSections">Sections with usable voting logs</span><strong id="coverage-ratio">—</strong></div><div class="coverage-track"><div id="coverage-track-fill"></div></div><div class="coverage-breakdown"><div><span class="green"></span><span data-i18n="included">Included in analysis</span><strong id="coverage-included">—</strong></div><div><span class="grey"></span><span data-i18n="remainingSections">Without a regular voting log</span><strong id="coverage-remaining">—</strong></div><div><span class="amber"></span><span data-i18n="flagged">Counter exceptions · bulletin totals retained</span><strong id="coverage-flagged">—</strong></div></div><p data-i18n="coverageFoot">Aggregated polling sections are counted through their primary section, avoiding duplicate machine totals.</p></div></section>
  <section id="reproduce" class="wrap reproduce-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-index">05 /</span><h2 data-i18n="reproduceTitle">Reproduce this analysis yourself</h2></div><a href="/reproduce.py" class="outline-button" download data-i18n="downloadPython">↓ Download the Python script</a></div><p class="reproduce-intro" data-i18n="reproduceIntro">Do not take our word for it. The source files are public. This standalone script downloads the same inputs, analyses them and writes the results on your own computer.</p><div class="reproduce-steps"><article><span class="step-number">1</span><div><h3 data-i18n="reproStep1">Download the script</h3><p data-i18n="reproCopy1">You need Python 3.10 or newer. No API key, account, proxy, package installation or website code is required.</p><a href="/reproduce.py" download>reproduce.py ↓</a></div></article><article><span class="step-number">2</span><div><h3 data-i18n="reproStep2">Run it in a terminal</h3><p data-i18n="reproCopy2">The full run uses one thread and one sequential internet connection. Allow at least 100 GB of free disk space for the relevant raw archives. It can take a long time; rerunning the same command resumes saved work.</p><div class="code-block"><code>python3 reproduce.py --database brazil-2026.sqlite --output results.json</code><button id="copy-command" aria-label="Copy command">⧉</button></div><p class="small-note" data-i18n="reproSelfTest">Optional offline check first: python3 reproduce.py --self-test</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">3</span><div><h3 data-i18n="reproStep3">Inspect the outputs</h3><p data-i18n="reproCopy3">The SQLite file preserves downloaded archives, source URLs, checksums and checkpoints. The JSON output reports observed time buckets, geographic totals, official candidate totals, excluded sections and the difference from the official turnout. Partial runs are labelled partial.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">4</span><div><h3 data-i18n="reproStep4">Check the exact source requests</h3><p data-i18n="reproCopy4">Polling event 3221 is the October 25 second round. Presidential result 6258 provides the official benchmark. For each primary section, read its metadata, then download the advertised log and bulletin under the published hash.</p><div class="source-links"><a href="https://resultados.tse.jus.br/oficial/ele2026/arquivo-urna/3221/config/df/df-p003221-cs.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="indexExample">1. Example: official section index ↗</a><a href="https://resultados.tse.jus.br/oficial/ele2026/arquivo-urna/3221/dados/df/97012/0001/0001/p003221-df-m97012-z0001-s0001-aux.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="auxExample">2. Example: section file metadata ↗</a><a id="example-log-link" href="https://resultados.tse.jus.br/oficial/ele2026/arquivo-urna/3221/dados/df/97012/0001/0001/436858652d35384167714e6f65684166662b417164726b4759494c333578744b4f577961485153544c70453d/o03221df9701200010001-log.jez" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="logExample">3. Example: actual machine-log archive ↗</a><a href="https://resultados.tse.jus.br/oficial/ele2026/6258/dados/br/br-c0001-e006258-u.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="benchmarkExample">4. Official nationwide result JSON ↗</a><a href="/data/summary.json" target="_blank" data-i18n="ourSnapshot">5. Our exact published aggregate snapshot ↗</a><a href="/data/official-results.json" target="_blank" data-i18n="officialSnapshot">6. Official totals and source URLs used here ↗</a><a href="/data/reconciliation.json" target="_blank" data-i18n="reconciliationSnapshot">7. All 5,757 municipality reconciliations ↗</a><a href="/data/untimed-sections.json" target="_blank" data-i18n="untimedSnapshot">8. Source-backed untimed ballot supplements ↗</a></div></div></article></div><div class="candidate-time-note"><strong data-i18n="candidateTimeTitle">Why there is no candidate-by-time split</strong><p data-i18n="candidateTimeCopy">The public machine logs record voting events, not candidate choices. The digital vote records are randomized to protect ballot secrecy. Neither this site nor the script can reconstruct how many votes for each candidate were cast before or after 5 p.m. Candidate totals come from official result bulletins and are shown separately from the time analysis.</p></div></section>
  <section id="methodology" class="method-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-index">04 /</span><h2 data-i18n="methodTitle">Sources and methodology</h2></div><span class="method-label" data-i18n="methodTag">REPRODUCIBLE · AGGREGATED · SOURCE-LINKED</span></div><div class="method-grid"><article><span class="method-number">01</span><h3 data-i18n="sourceTitle">Start with the source</h3><p data-i18n="sourceCopy">Download the official TSE logs for each primary polling section in the October 25 second round. Preserve source URLs and checksums; validate each compressed archive.</p><a href="https://resultados.tse.jus.br/oficial/app/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="sourceLink">Explore TSE machine files ↗</a></article><article><span class="method-number">02</span><h3 data-i18n="countTitle">Count, then reconcile</h3><p data-i18n="countCopy">Count presidential confirmations and suspension-assigned null ballots, including archived log segments. Deduplicate exact events and reconcile each section against completed voting records.</p><a href="https://www.tse.jus.br/eleicoes/eleicoes-2026-content/arquivos/log-do-ecossistema" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="countLink">Read the TSE log specification ↗</a></article><article><span class="method-number">03</span><h3 data-i18n="timeTitle">Put every clock on one timeline</h3><p data-i18n="timeCopy">Convert domestic machine-clock times to Brasília time, accounting for Acre, western Amazonas and Fernando de Noronha. Overseas timestamps remain unclassified until verified.</p><a href="https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2026/Setembro/faltam-26-dias-votacao-comeca-e-termina-no-mesmo-horario-em-todo-o-pais" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n="timeLink">See official voting time zones ↗</a></article></div><details class="method-details"><summary><span data-i18n="technicalTitle">Definitions, limitations and exact time boundaries</span><span>+</span></summary><div><p data-i18n="technical1">Before 5 p.m.: timestamp &lt; 17:00. 5–7 p.m.: 17:00 ≤ timestamp &lt; 19:00. At / after 7 p.m.: timestamp ≥ 19:00. Unclassified times are retained as a separate bucket. These four buckets always add to the displayed total.</p><p data-i18n="technical2">Timestamps come from voting-machine system clocks. They describe recorded ballot events, not a voter’s arrival time. Clock adjustments and missing archived segments may affect interpretation. These aggregates do not identify a voter’s candidate choice.</p><p data-i18n="technical3">This independent analysis is not an official TSE result or a finding of electoral irregularity. Votes recorded after the original close cannot, by timing alone, be attributed to the extension. Partial coverage is not a representative sample and must not be extrapolated to all voters.</p><p data-i18n="technical4">Recorded SHA-256 checksums and ZIP checks preserve and check the downloaded files; they do not constitute verification of the TSE’s separate digital-signature envelopes. The public site contains aggregate statistics only.</p><p><span data-i18n="geographySource">Map source:</span> <a href="https://geoftp.ibge.gov.br/organizacao_do_territorio/malhas_territoriais/malhas_municipais/municipio_2024/Brasil/BR_UF_2024.zip" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IBGE · BR_UF_2024</a></p></div></details></div></section>
